  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: Online therapy is not second-best — for many people it works better
    metin: Some clients find it easier to open up on video than in a clinical room. The home environment feels safer; there is no travel anxiety before a session; and clients in rural parts of North Cyprus can access the same quality of support as those in Famagusta city centre. The research consistently supports these observations.
  - type: kart-yigini
    baslik: Who is online therapy best suited for in North Cyprus?
    kartlar:
      - baslik: '[International students](/en/blog/mental-health-international-students-famagusta.html) and university residents'
        metin: Living on or near campus, with unpredictable schedules and no private transport, online sessions eliminate the commute and fit around lectures, exams and part-time work.
      - baslik: Expats and long-term residents
        metin: Accessing English-language therapy in a small territory is already difficult. Online sessions open up the option of working with a qualified English-speaking psychologist in Famagusta regardless of where in TRNC you live.
      - baslik: People with busy or shift-based schedules
        metin: Without the 20–30 minutes of travel time each way, online therapy is easier to fit into demanding working weeks. Early morning, lunchtime and evening slots become practical in a way they are not with in-person sessions.
      - baslik: Those with social anxiety or health concerns
        metin: For people whose anxiety makes public spaces difficult, or who have physical health conditions affecting travel, online therapy removes a significant practical barrier to starting.
  - type: metin
    baslik: Privacy and confidentiality in online sessions
    metin: |-
      We use end-to-end encrypted video platforms for all online sessions. Sessions are never recorded. No information about your attendance or content is shared with any third party, including your university, employer or family, except in the narrow legal circumstances that apply to all therapy.

      If you are concerned about privacy at your end — for instance, a shared student flat — using headphones and taking the session from a private space (car, library study room, outdoor setting) is usually sufficient.
  - type: onayli-liste
    baslik: 'Getting started: booking your first online session'
    maddeler:
      - baslik: 'Step 1: Message us on WhatsApp'
        aciklama: Send us a brief message introducing yourself and what you are looking for. No referral needed, no waiting list.
      - baslik: 'Step 2: Book your first session'
        aciklama: We schedule your first full session, confirm your preferred video platform, and send the secure link in advance.
      - baslik: 'Step 3: Join from anywhere in TRNC'
        aciklama: Your room, your office, your car — wherever gives you 50 minutes of privacy. Stable internet and headphones are all you need.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: turuncu
    baslik: When is in-person therapy recommended instead?
    metin: For most concerns, online therapy is equally effective. In-person sessions may be preferable for certain trauma-processing techniques, for clients who find technology frustrating, or for those who value the ritual of leaving home for a session. We offer both formats — and in some cases, a mix of the two.
